.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH tapectl-key 1  "tapectl-key " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-key \- Manage encryption keys
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl key\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage encryption keys
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, receipts. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, receipts, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
tapectl\-key\-generate(1)
Generate a new keypair for a tenant, or the permanent escrow recipient with \-\-escrow (ADR\-0005)
.TP
tapectl\-key\-list(1)
List keys for a tenant
.TP
tapectl\-key\-export(1)
Export a public key to stdout
.TP
tapectl\-key\-rotate(1)
Rotate keys for a tenant (deactivate old, generate new). Refuses unless a permanent escrow recipient is registered (ADR\-0005); never deactivates or replaces the escrow key itself
.TP
tapectl\-key\-import(1)
Import a public key from a file, or adopt an existing one as the permanent escrow recipient with \-\-escrow (ADR\-0005)
.TP
tapectl\-key\-escrow\-kit(1)
Generate the printed Heir Kit and the encrypted catalog bundle (ADR\-0005 / ADR\-0009, issue #69)
.TP
tapectl\-key\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
